{"v":1,"book":"gita","n":1,"title":"Arjuna’s Dilemma","narrator":{"name":"Brian","voice":"en-US-BrianMultilingualNeural"},"duration":305.064,"scenes":[{"layout":"title","headline":"Arjuna’s Dilemma","visual":["Where the Gita begins: on a battlefield"],"L":[],"say":"Chapter One. Arjuna's Dilemma. The Bhagavad-Gita does not begin in a temple or a forest. It begins on a battlefield, a few moments before a war.","start":0.0,"at":0.576,"end":11.784,"words":[[0.05,0.4,"Chapter"],[0.463,0.35,"One"],[1.175,0.525,"Arjuna's"],[1.712,0.588,"Dilemma"],[2.688,0.075,"The"],[2.775,0.775,"Bhagavad-Gita"],[3.562,0.175,"does"],[3.75,0.287,"not"],[4.05,0.45,"begin"],[4.513,0.15,"in"],[4.675,0.075,"a"],[4.763,0.512,"temple"],[5.287,0.188,"or"],[5.487,0.062,"a"],[5.562,0.65,"forest"],[6.612,0.113,"It"],[6.737,0.45,"begins"],[7.2,0.138,"on"],[7.35,0.075,"a"],[7.438,0.787,"battlefield"],[8.25,0.087,"a"],[8.35,0.237,"few"],[8.6,0.45,"moments"],[9.062,0.35,"before"],[9.425,0.087,"a"],[9.525,0.438,"war"]]},{"layout":"story","headline":"Two families, one kingdom","visual":["The Pandavas and the Kauravas are cousins","The Kauravas took the kingdom by deceit","Every attempt at peace has failed"],"L":[],"beyond":true,"say":"First, the background, which comes from the Mahabharata, the great epic the Gita belongs to, and not from our book. Two branches of one royal family, the five Pandava brothers and the hundred Kaurava brothers, both claim the kingdom. The Kauravas cheated the Pandavas out of it, sent them into exile, and refused to return even five villages. Krishna himself went to plead for peace, and was turned away.","start":11.784,"at":12.36,"end":38.712,"words":[[0.087,0.537,"First"],[0.65,0.125,"the"],[0.787,0.625,"background"],[1.438,0.188,"which"],[1.637,0.263,"comes"],[1.913,0.163,"from"],[2.087,0.062,"the"],[2.163,0.762,"Mahabharata"],[2.95,0.1,"the"],[3.062,0.3,"great"],[3.375,0.35,"epic"],[3.737,0.087,"the"],[3.837,0.3,"Gita"],[4.15,0.45,"belongs"],[4.612,0.25,"to"],[4.888,0.163,"a