ge"],[3.025,0.375,"asks"],[3.413,0.15,"his"],[3.575,0.7,"charioteer"],[4.287,0.087,"and"],[4.388,0.5,"friend"],[5.162,0.55,"Krishna"],[6.2,0.1,"to"],[6.312,0.338,"drive"],[6.662,0.075,"the"],[6.75,0.5,"chariot"],[7.263,0.212,"into"],[7.487,0.062,"the"],[7.562,0.338,"open"],[7.912,0.388,"ground"],[8.312,0.287,"between"],[8.613,0.075,"the"],[8.7,0.212,"two"],[8.925,0.512,"armies"],[9.85,0.163,"so"],[10.025,0.125,"he"],[10.162,0.113,"can"],[10.287,0.3,"see"],[10.6,0.138,"who"],[10.75,0.113,"he"],[10.875,0.275,"must"],[11.162,0.375,"fight"],[11.938,0.113,"And"],[12.062,0.2,"there"],[12.275,0.125,"he"],[12.412,0.325,"sees"],[12.75,0.325,"them"],[13.262,0.5,"his"],[13.775,0.613,"grandfather"],[14.4,0.5,"Bhishma"],[14.912,0.225,"his"],[15.15,0.325,"teacher"],[15.488,0.487,"Drona"],[16.5,0.6,"uncles"],[17.275,0.613,"cousins"],[18.3,0.637,"friends"],[19.312,0.613,"Compassion"],[19.938,0.412,"floods"],[20.363,0.388,"him"],[21.25,0.175,"His"],[21.438,0.312,"mouth"],[21.762,0.237,"goes"],[22.012,0.475,"dry"],[22.5,0.35,"his"],[22.863,0.338,"limbs"],[23.212,0.55,"tremble"],[24.2,0.113,"and"],[24.325,0.15,"his"],[24.488,0.338,"great"],[24.837,0.225,"bow"],[25.075,0.463,"slips"],[25.55,0.15,"from"],[25.712,0.125,"his"],[25.85,0.438,"hand"]]},{"layout":"story","headline":"The case against fighting","visual":["What good is a kingdom won by killing family?","War destroys families and their traditions","Better to be killed than to kill them"],"L":[],"beyond":true,"say":"In the full Gita, Arjuna then argues at length, and our book summarises his words. What good is a kingdom, he asks, if it is won by killing the very people we wanted to share it with? War destroys families, and with them their traditions and their sense of right. It would be better, he says, to be killed unarmed than to raise a weapon against them.","start":91.44,"at":92.016,"end":114.48,"words":[[0.087,0.1,"In"],[0.2,0.087,"the"],[0.3,0.275,"full"],[0.588,0.512,"Gita"],[1.3,0.537,"Arjuna"],[1.85,0.237,"then"],[2.1,0.45,"argues"],[2.562,0.138,"at"],[2.712,0.5,"length"],[3.5,0.212,"and"],[3.725,0.138,"our"],[3.875,0.212,"book"],[4.1,0.688,"summarises"],[4.8,0.175,"his"],[4.987,0.525,"words"],[5.9,0.188,"What"],[6.1,0.175,"good"],[6.287,0.113,"is"],[6.412,0.075,"a"],[6.5,0.5,"kingdom"],[7.025,0.225,"he"],[7.263,0.537,"asks"],[8.075,0.2,"if"],[8.287,0.075,"it"],[8.375,0.138,"is"],[8.525,0.275,"won"],[8.812,0.175,"by"],[9.0,0.425,"killing"],[9.438,0.075,"the"],[9.525,0.25,"very"],[9.787,0.338,"people"],[10.137,0.113,"we"],[10.262,0.287,"wanted"],[10.562,0.087,"to"],[10.662,0.3,"share"],[10.975,0.1,"it"],[11.088,0.3,"with"],[11.8,0.312,"War"],[12.125,0.562,"destroys"],[12.7,0.662,"families"],[13.65,0.25,"and"],[13.912,0.2,"with"],[14.125,0.287,"them"],[14.425,0.175,"their"],[14.613,0.713,"traditions"],[15.338,0.163,"and"],[15.512,0.138,"their"],[15.662,0.3,"sense"],[15.975,0.125,"of"],[16.113,0.375,"right"],[16.85,0.15,"It"],[17.012,0.138,"would"],[17.163,0.15,"be"],[17.325,0.375,"better"],[17.725,0.138,"he"],[17.875,0.362,"says"],[18.262,0.113,"to"],[18.387,0.125,"be"],[18.525,0.375,"killed"],[18.925,0.625,"unarmed"],[19.575,0.163,"than"],[19.75,0.113,"to"],[19.875,0.275,"raise"],[20.163,0.075,"a"],[20.25,0.312,"weapon"],[20.575,0.388,"against"],[20.975,0.263,"them"]]},{"layout":"verse","headline":"","visual":[],"L":["L3"],"ref":"1.47","verse":"Arjuna sat down on the back seat of the chariot with his mind overwhelmed with sorrow.","key":false,"vs":[23,39],"say":"And the chapter ends with one of the most honest images in all of scripture: a hero who cannot go on. Verse forty-seven. Arjuna sat down on the back seat of the chariot with his mind overwhelmed with sorrow.","start":114.48,"at":115.056,"end":130.008,"words":[[0.087,0.113,"And"],[0.212,0.075,"the"],[0.3,0.512,"chapter"],[0.825,0.338,"ends"],[1.175,0.175,"with"],[1.363,0.175,"one"],[1.55,0.075,"of"],[1.637,0.075,"the"],[1.725,0.287,"most"],[2.038,0.412,"honest"],[2.462,0.487,"images"],[2.962,0.163,"in"],[3.138,0.225,"all"],[3.375,0.062,"of"],[3.45,0.6,"scripture"],[4.675,0.087,"a"],[4.775,0.4,"hero"],[5.188,0.138,"who"],[5.338,0.35,"cannot"],[5.7,0.188,"go"],[5.9,0.3,"on"],[6.588,0.388,"Verse"],[6.987,0.838,"forty-seven"],[8.225,0.475,"Arjuna"],[8.713,0.312,"sat"],[9.037,0.35,"down"],[9.4,0.125,"on"],[9.537,0.1,"the"],[9.65,0.275,"back"],[9.938,0.325,"seat"],[10.275,0.075,"of"],[10.363,0.075,"the"],[10.45,0.55,"chariot"],[11.012,0.113,"with"],[11.137,0.15,"his"],[11.3,0.463,"mind"],[11.787,0.688,"overwhelmed"],[12.488,0.138,"with"],[12.637,0.512,"sorrow"]]},{"layout":"compare","headline":"The two pulls on Arjuna","visual":["Duty | Emotion","Fight for justice | Love for his relatives","Protect the innocent | Spare his teachers","The role of a warrior | The heart of a grandson"],"L":["L1"],"say":"Lesson one. Duty versus emotion, and both matter. Arjuna is pulled between what he should do, which is to fight for justice, and what he feels, which is love for the people on the other side. The chapter does not mock his feelings. The lesson is to acknowledge both, and to dismiss neither.","start":130.008,"at":130.584,"end":149.52,"words":[[0.062,0.35,"Lesson"],[0.425,0.375,"one"],[1.188,0.3,"Duty"],[1.5,0.425,"versus"],[1.938,0.65,"emotion"],[2.612,0.225,"and"],[2.85,0.275,"both"],[3.138,0.487,"matter"],[4.025,0.463,"Arjuna"],[4.5,0.163,"is"],[4.675,0.338,"pulled"],[5.025,0.388,"between"],[5.425,0.138,"what"],[5.575,0.1,"he"],[5.688,0.212,"should"],[5.912,0.287,"do"],[6.225,0.212,"which"],[6.45,0.125,"is"],[6.588,0.1,"to"],[6.7,0.325,"fight"],[7.037,0.113,"for"],[7.162,0.625,"justice"],[8.012,0.225,"and"],[8.25,0.138,"what"],[8.4,0.138,"he"],[8.55,0.487,"feels"],[9.062,0.2,"which"],[9.275,0.15,"is"],[9.438,0.312,"love"],[9.762,0.125,"for"],[9.9,0.087,"the"],[10.0,0.338,"people"],[10.35,0.1,"on"],[10.463,0.075,"the"],[10.55,0.2,"other"],[10.762,0.45,"side"],[11.6,0.062,"The"],[11.675,0.512,"chapter"],[12.2,0.175,"does"],[12.387,0.275,"not"],[12.675,0.275,"mock"],[12.963,0.188,"his"],[13.162,0.625,"feelings"],[14.175,0.087,"The"],[14.275,0.412,"lesson"],[14.7,0.212,"is"],[14.925,0.138,"to"],[15.075,0.55,"acknowledge"],[15.637,0.487,"both"],[16.325,0.212,"and"],[16.55,0.138,"to"],[16.7,0.5,"dismiss"],[17.212,0.487,"neither"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"Ignorance Is Not Bliss—Face Reality","visual":["Arjuna looked and recognised the people he loved","He could not unsee it","Facing a hard truth is the first step"],"L":["L2"],"say":"Lesson two. Ignorance is not bliss, so face reality. Arjuna chose to drive into the middle and look. Once he saw the faces of the people he loved, he could not unsee them. Don't avoid difficult truths. Facing reality, even when it hurts, is the first step toward wisdom.","start":149.52,"at":150.096,"end":170.544,"words":[[0.062,0.338,"Lesson"],[0.412,0.375,"two"],[1.15,0.512,"Ignorance"],[1.675,0.125,"is"],[1.812,0.287,"not"],[2.112,0.388,"bliss"],[2.513,0.212,"so"],[2.737,0.338,"face"],[3.087,0.613,"reality"],[4.075,0.425,"Arjuna"],[4.513,0.438,"chose"],[4.963,0.113,"to"],[5.088,0.45,"drive"],[5.55,0.263,"into"],[5.825,0.087,"the"],[5.925,0.388,"middle"],[6.325,0.15,"and"],[6.487,0.438,"look"],[7.338,0.338,"Once"],[7.688,0.125,"he"],[7.825,0.312,"saw"],[8.15,0.1,"the"],[8.262,0.537,"faces"],[8.812,0.1,"of"],[8.925,0.087,"the"],[9.025,0.325,"people"],[9.363,0.125,"he"],[9.5,0.512,"loved"],[10.363,0.412,"he"],[10.787,0.15,"could"],[10.95,0.263,"not"],[11.225,0.4,"unsee"],[11.637,0.3,"them"],[12.312,0.237,"Don't"],[12.562,0.45,"avoid"],[13.025,0.45,"difficult"],[13.488,0.562,"truths"],[14.45,0.388,"Facing"],[14.85,0.675,"reality"],[15.863,0.325,"even"],[16.2,0.15,"when"],[16.363,0.075,"it"],[16.45,0.55,"hurts"],[17.375,0.2,"is"],[17.587,0.1,"the"],[17.7,0.325,"first"],[18.038,0.312,"step"],[18.363,0.312,"toward"],[18.688,0.512,"wisdom"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"It's Okay to Doubt and Feel Lost","visual":["Arjuna admits he does not know what to do","He does not pretend to be brave","Doubt is honest, not weak"],"L":["L3"],"s