s not","Kindness never requires abandoning what is right"],"L":["L7"],"say":"Lesson seven. Compassion doesn't mean avoiding hard choices. Arjuna's love for the people across the field is real and good. But it cannot be a reason to let injustice stand. Being kind and caring never requires you to abandon what is right.","start":246.936,"at":247.512,"end":264.528,"words":[[0.062,0.338,"Lesson"],[0.412,0.55,"seven"],[1.337,0.625,"Compassion"],[1.975,0.312,"doesn't"],[2.3,0.3,"mean"],[2.625,0.5,"avoiding"],[3.138,0.287,"hard"],[3.438,0.637,"choices"],[4.475,0.525,"Arjuna's"],[5.013,0.388,"love"],[5.425,0.15,"for"],[5.588,0.087,"the"],[5.688,0.375,"people"],[6.075,0.425,"across"],[6.513,0.087,"the"],[6.612,0.438,"field"],[7.062,0.2,"is"],[7.275,0.388,"real"],[7.675,0.15,"and"],[7.838,0.388,"good"],[8.613,0.113,"But"],[8.738,0.113,"it"],[8.863,0.388,"cannot"],[9.262,0.15,"be"],[9.425,0.062,"a"],[9.5,0.475,"reason"],[9.988,0.15,"to"],[10.15,0.237,"let"],[10.4,0.562,"injustice"],[10.975,0.512,"stand"],[11.887,0.212,"Being"],[12.113,0.537,"kind"],[12.662,0.15,"and"],[12.825,0.412,"caring"],[13.25,0.338,"never"],[13.6,0.537,"requires"],[14.15,0.188,"you"],[14.35,0.163,"to"],[14.525,0.512,"abandon"],[15.05,0.15,"what"],[15.213,0.138,"is"],[15.363,0.412,"right"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"The Beginning of Wisdom Is Admitting What You Don't Know","visual":["\"I don't know what to do\"","That admission opens the door to the teaching","Humility is where learning begins"],"L":["L8"],"say":"Lesson eight. The beginning of wisdom is admitting what you don't know. Arjuna lays down his weapons and says, in effect, I don't know what to do. That admission opens the door to everything Krishna is about to teach. Confidence without wisdom is dangerous. Humility is where learning begins.","start":264.528,"at":265.104,"end":285.168,"words":[[0.062,0.362,"Lesson"],[0.438,0.325,"eight"],[1.15,0.075,"The"],[1.238,0.4,"beginning"],[1.65,0.138,"of"],[1.8,0.512,"wisdom"],[2.337,0.188,"is"],[2.5